= Probability — Technical =

== Probability space ==
A probability space is:

<pre>
(Ω, F, P)
</pre>

where:

* Ω is the sample space;
* F is a sigma-algebra of events;
* P is a probability measure.

The measure satisfies non-negativity, normalization, and countable additivity.

== Countable additivity ==
For pairwise disjoint events Aᵢ:

<pre>
P(⋃ Aᵢ) = Σ P(Aᵢ)
</pre>

This extends finite additivity to countable collections.

== Random variables ==
A random variable is a measurable function from Ω into a value space.

Its induced [[Probability distribution]] describes probabilities over values rather than directly over elementary outcomes.

== Interpretation layer ==
The axioms constrain numerical coherence but do not uniquely determine whether probabilities represent frequencies, propensities, credences, or logical support.

